From e67224c9b254b23fa18c7ceb061171d81477ae39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:34:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/54] moe cache RAM tier: a partial tier per layer when the
 full tier does not fit the pin budget (GGML_MOE_TIER_SHARE)

When the full tier of every sparse table exceeds the pin budget, every layer gets an equal share of it (the budget less
GGML_MOE_TIER_REG_HEADROOM_MIB, default 10 %), the same expert count for each of its tables, holding the hottest cold
experts by the heat prior (ties by expert id).  A cold expert outside the tier is read through the registered file
alias (registered on demand, as a table without a tier), an admission of one fills from the alias, and a victim with
no free RAM slot goes back to the file (its cold pointer only).  The file pages stay cached while a partial tier reads
them, and a partial tier is not device-remapped (the eager path registers its cold experts before the read).
GGML_MOE_TIER_SHARE=0: the previous all-or-nothing tier per table.
